looking for safety codes?

00:03:48.936 --> 00:03:50.328
Cause they're really hard to find,

00:03:50.328 --> 00:03:52.614
and hardly anybody ever finds it.

00:03:52.614 --> 00:03:54.979
- Nah, I'm all good on codes so...

00:03:54.979 --> 00:03:56.947
- I mean I can help
you with anything else.

00:03:56.947 --> 00:03:59.279
- I'm good, thanks.

00:03:59.279 --> 00:04:00.446
- You sure?

00:04:02.675 --> 00:04:04.322
- Alright we have coir
rope, nautical rope,

00:04:04.322 --> 00:04:07.405
torn rope, polypropylene
rope, parachute rope,

00:04:07.405 --> 00:04:08.838
twine rope, rope twine, pretty much

00:04:08.838 --> 00:04:11.249
everything you ever need.

00:04:11.249 --> 00:04:13.748
- I had no idea there were
this many kinds of rope.

00:04:13.748 --> 00:04:16.037
- May I ask what you need it for sir?

00:04:16.037 --> 00:04:18.120
- Just a good house rope.

00:04:18.981 --> 00:04:20.175
- Oh, a house rope?

00:04:20.175 --> 00:04:21.889
So you're doing some remodeling?

00:04:21.889 --> 00:04:24.035
- Yeah, you know, I mean I have like

00:04:24.035 --> 00:04:25.834
a hammer and a drill, and I feel like

00:04:25.834 --> 00:04:27.806
I need a good rope in the kit.

00:04:27.806 --> 00:04:31.973
- Okay, well we have this
nice general purpose rope.

00:04:34.685 --> 00:04:37.880
- Probably need something
a little more substantial.

00:04:37.880 --> 00:04:40.237
- Okay, well we can do that.

00:04:40.237 --> 00:04:42.393
Let's see...

00:04:42.393 --> 00:04:44.970
- Just in case there's and
earthquake or something.

00:04:44.970 --> 00:04:49.911
I might need to kick open
a door and repel to safety.

00:04:49.911 --> 00:04:53.595
- So a rope that can hold
your own body weight?

00:04:53.595 --> 00:04:56.581
- Yeah, that would be perfect actually.

00:04:56.581 --> 00:04:59.164
- What do you weigh, about 175?

00:05:00.253 --> 00:05:01.836
- 155.

00:05:03.482 --> 00:05:08.365
- Well, we have this nice climbing rope.

00:05:08.365 --> 00:05:10.615
(whirring)

00:05:13.303 --> 00:05:14.817
- Do you have anything less colorful?

00:05:14.817 --> 00:05:15.957
You know, something they would use

00:05:15.957 --> 00:05:19.563
to tie people down to train
tracks back in the old days?

00:05:19.563 --> 00:05:23.730
- Okay, natural fiber rope.

00:05:26.509 --> 00:05:28.842
- Perfect.

00:05:34.313 --> 00:05:36.563
- I know what you're doin'.

00:05:38.805 --> 00:05:40.161
- Okay?

00:05:40.161 --> 00:05:41.411
- I respect it.

00:05:42.610 --> 00:05:44.862
Taking your life in your own hands,

00:05:44.862 --> 00:05:47.643
wanting to get out
while you're at the top.

00:05:47.643 --> 00:05:49.640
Everything's fucked anyways.

00:05:49.640 --> 00:05:52.807
Who says quantity over quality, right?

00:05:54.162 --> 00:05:56.745
Have you ever seen a dead body?

00:05:57.997 --> 00:05:59.901
- No.

00:05:59.901 --> 00:06:02.160
- I was in the army back in the day.

00:06:02.160 --> 00:06:03.591
- Thank you for your service.

00:06:03.591 --> 00:06:07.908
- Nah, I wasn't exactly on
the front lines, I was a cook.

00:06:07.908 --> 00:06:12.621
Anyways, there was this
PFC, he was on kitchen duty.

00:06:12.621 --> 00:06:15.287
Found out he couldn't take it anymore.

00:06:15.287 --> 00:06:18.335
Got drunk while on fire watch,

00:06:18.335 --> 00:06:21.136
found out that we didn't
lock the gas ovens,

00:06:21.136 --> 00:06:24.386
and... boom.

00:06:25.886 --> 00:06:29.726
'Cause who in the hell wanna
fuck with an oven, right?

00:06:29.726 --> 00:06:30.559
- Yeah.

00:06:30.559 --> 00:06:34.543
- You know people shit
themselves when they die?

00:06:34.543 --> 00:06:36.499
- No, wait really?

00:06:36.499 --> 00:06:38.832
- It's a mess man.

00:06:42.964 --> 00:06:47.131
Hey, we got tarps on isle 39F.

00:06:50.431 --> 00:06:52.014
